 "text": "9/29/26, 9:48 AM\nThe Check Benefit Free Period operation provides information about benefit-free periods. Benefit-free periods occur for an\n\ninsurance contract if open items with a due date in the past are dunned, for example, and dunning levels defined in Customizing\nare reached within the corresponding dunning procedure.\n\nYou can Use the Check Benefit Free Period operation in claim processing to check whether the insurer has to settle the claim or\nwhether the insurer is benefit-free at the time where the claim happened due to missing payments from the customer.\n\nFeatures\n\nThe selection is done by the Insurance Contract Reference ID element, which is the internal ID of the underlying insurance object\nin Colletions/Disbursements. The operation returns the periods, in which the insurance contract was or is benefit-free.\n\nNote:\n\nThe benefit-free periods are defined via dunning level categories. The dunning levels with dunning level categories 05 (benefit-\nfree), 08 (legal proceedings - with automatic clearing), or O9 (legal proceedings - without automatic clearing) are regarded as\n\nbenefit-free. The creation data of the dunning notice represents the start of the benefit-free period.\n\nError Handling\n\nError messages are returned in the error log.\n\nMessage Types\n\ne InsuranceContractBenefitFreePeriodBylnsuranceContractIDAndClaimPeriodQuery\n\ne InsuranceContractBenefitFreePeriodBylnsuranceContractIDAndClaimPeriodResponse\n\nPrerequisites\n\nYou can only use the Check Benefit Free Period operation if the business function SAP for Insurance:\nCollections/Disbursements 1 is active and if the dunning by dunning procedure for insurance companies is used.\n\nConstraints\n\nYou can only use the Check Benefit Free Period if you use the dunning by dunning procedures for insurance companies.\n\nNote that the start of the benefit-free period might be several days afterwards from a legal perspective, since it takes some days\nuntil the dunning letter reaches the customer and there might also be buffer for him to react.\n\nNotes on SAP Implementation\n\nConfiguration\n\nYou set the relevant dunning level categories in Customizing for Collections/Disbursements , under Business Transactions ->\nDunning -> Dunning by Dunning Procedure -> Configure Dunning Procedure . The dunning levels with dunning level categories\n05 (benefit-free), 08 (legal proceedings - with automatic clearing) or 09 (legal proceedings - without automatic clearing) are\nregarded as benefit-free.\n",
